From: Alex Rau <alex@retroduction.org>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 21:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: edma: no offload for RTL8_4-tagged
 frames

DSA user ports inherit the conduit's checksum and segmentation offload
features. A frame sent through a user port therefore reaches the EDMA
with CHECKSUM_PARTIAL, after the tagger has put its tag in front of the
ethertype. With the RTL8_4 tag (Realtek RTL8365MB, RTL8372N) the EDMA
cannot find the L3/L4 headers and sends the frame with a wrong
checksum, so the router's own TCP and UDP traffic through the switch
fails while ICMP and forwarded traffic still work.

Drop checksum and GSO offload for such frames in ndo_features_check, so
the stack does both in software. RTL8_4T is not affected: its tagger
checksums in software before appending the trailer.

Switch drivers used to work around this by clearing the conduit's
checksum features in their setup, but edma_port_open() sets them again
whenever the conduit opens, so the workaround depended on the order of
switch setup and conduit open.

Same approach as OpenWrt's mtk_eth_soc fix
739-net-ethernet-mtk_eth_soc-fix-offload-with-incompatible-.patch.

Tested on the UniFi Cloud Gateway Fiber (IPQ9574, RTL8372N, RTL8_4 tag):
SSH, HTTP and DNS to the router work right after boot and after
eth0 down/up, without clearing the conduit features by hand; 300 MB
TCP from the router at 557 Mbit/s.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Alex Rau <alex@retroduction.org>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma_port.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma_port.c
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 #include <linux/of_net.h>
 #include <linux/phylink.h>
 #include <linux/printk.h>
+#include <net/dsa.h>
 
 #include "edma.h"
 #include "edma_cfg_rx.h"
@@ -177,10 +178,26 @@ static int edma_port_change_mtu(struct n
 	return ppe_port_set_maxframe(port_priv->ppe_port, mtu);
 }
 
-static netdev_features_t edma_port_feature_check(__maybe_unused struct sk_buff *skb,
-						 __maybe_unused struct net_device *netdev,
+static netdev_features_t edma_port_feature_check(struct sk_buff *skb,
+						 struct net_device *netdev,
 						 netdev_features_t features)
 {
+	/* Only frames that ask for checksum or segmentation offload matter */
+	if (skb->ip_summed != CHECKSUM_PARTIAL)
+		return features;
+
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_NET_DSA)
+	/* The RTL8_4 tag sits in front of the ethertype, so the EDMA cannot
+	 * find the L3/L4 headers and sends the frame with a wrong checksum.
+	 * Let the stack checksum and segment such frames in software.
+	 * RTL8_4T is not affected: its tagger checksums in software before
+	 * appending the trailer.
+	 */
+	if (netdev_uses_dsa(netdev) &&
+	    netdev->dsa_ptr->tag_ops->proto == DSA_TAG_PROTO_RTL8_4)
+		features &= ~(NETIF_F_CSUM_MASK | NETIF_F_GSO_MASK);
+#endif
+
 	return features;
 }
 
